course: dictionary
lesson: 13031
title: Fallen and the word fall
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fall is a verb that means to drop or go down. Its shapes are fall, falls, fell, fallen and falling. Fallen is the one you use after has, have, had or be: «The cup has fallen.»
explain: Fell and fallen are different. «The leaf fell yesterday» uses fell on its own. «The leaf has fallen» uses fallen after has. Never write «has fell».
explain: Fallen can also describe a thing. «The fallen leaves crunched under our feet» tells you the leaves have dropped to the ground. A fallen tree is a tree that has come down.
fact: Fallen is the form of fall used after has, have, had or be.
fact: «The temperature has fallen» means it went down, so it got colder.
fact: «Prices have fallen» means the numbers got smaller.
fact: A fallen power line or fallen tree can be dangerous: keep away and tell an adult.
fact: Fallen can also mean soldiers who died in a war, as in «the fallen».
exercise: «Sam has ___ over in the playground.» Which word fits? | fall | fell | falling | *fallen
exercise: «The apple ___ from the tree last night.» Which word fits? | falling | falls | fallen | *fell
exercise: «The fallen tree blocked the road.» What has fallen? | The wind | The sky | The road | *The tree
test: «Mia had ___ asleep before the film ended.» Which word fits? | *fallen | fell | falls | fall
test: Someone sees a fallen power line. What should they do? | Pick it up and move it out of the way | *Keep well away and tell an adult | Touch it to see if it is live | Stand under it to wait
exam: «Ben had ___ over on the ice and grazed his knee.» Which word fits? | *fallen | fell | fall | falling
